# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Spring Framework 6.2.19 (cart, orders, ui) — fix only in 7.x
# Fix requires Spring Boot 3.5 -> 4.x major migration (application code
# changes). Out of scope for capstone ("application development is not
# assessed"). Tracked as backlog item: "Upgrade Java services to Spring Boot 4".
#
# CVE-2026-47884 (CRITICAL) RCE via XsltView path handling
#   Not exploitable: no service uses XsltView/XSLT rendering
#   (UI renders with Thymeleaf; cart and orders are JSON REST APIs).
#
# CVE-2026-47890 (CRITICAL) SSE stream corruption with view rendering
#   Not exploitable: cart/orders have no Server-Sent Events. UI chat uses SSE
#   for plain data only (no view rendering) and is disabled (chat.enabled=false).
#
# CVE-2026-47892 (CRITICAL) Header predicate bypass in WebFlux Functional Endpoints (ui)
#   Not exploitable: UI defines routes only with annotated @Controller classes;
#   no RouterFunction / RequestPredicates (functional endpoints) are used.
#   cart and orders do not use WebFlux.
#
# Raised by: zeyaulhaq (DevSecOps)   Approved by: Eugene (DevSecOps) in PR review
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-47892 exp:2026-11-30